{"occurrence_no":"1356451","record_type":"occ","collection_no":"151252","identified_name":"Protadelomys lugdunensis n. sp.","identified_rank":"species","accepted_name":"Protadelomys lugdunensis","accepted_rank":"species","accepted_no":"350388","early_interval":"Lutetian","max_ma":48.07,"min_ma":41.03,"reference_no":"61550","lng":"4.750000","lat":"45.866669","cc":"FR","state":"Rhone","latlng_basis":"based on nearby landmark","latlng_precision":"minutes","geogcomments":"\"The locality no longer exists. It was located in a western extension of the Mont d’Or lyonnais, a small limestone mount located 10 km north-northwest of Lyon, central eastern France (‘‘département’’, or administrative region, of Rhône). The fossils were recovered from a fissure-fill situated close to the\r\nhamlet of La Clôtre, near the village of Lissieu. The enclosing rocks, and therefore the fissure disappeared (mined out) by the end of the nineteenth century.\" - Rage and Auge (2010)","environment":"fissure fill","primary_reference":"B. Comte, M. Sabatier, and B. Marandat, M. Vianey-Liaud. 2012. Les rongeurs de Chéry-Chartreuve et Rocourt-Saint-Martin (est du bassin de Paris; Aisne, France). Leur place parmi les faunes de l'Eocène Moyen d'Europe. Palaeovertebrata 37(4-5):167-271","phylum":"Chordata","phylum_no":"33815","class":"Mammalia","class_no":"36651","order":"Rodentia","order_no":"41370","family":"Pseudosciuridae","family_no":"57354","genus":"Protadelomys","genus_no":"41986"},
