{"occurrence_no":"1370770","record_type":"occ","collection_no":"187095","identified_name":"Ammonites deshayesi n. sp.","identified_rank":"species","difference":"recombined as","accepted_name":"Deshayesites deshayesi","accepted_rank":"species","accepted_no":"130797","early_interval":"Early Aptian","max_ma":121.4,"min_ma":119.57,"reference_no":"62769","lng":"4.905000","lat":"48.455002","cc":"FR","latlng_basis":"based on nearby landmark","latlng_precision":"3","geogscale":"outcrop","geogcomments":"Most of the data about the Argiles à Plicatules and the related fossils deposited in public collections were obtained thanks to the numerous excavations made for extensive industrial exploitation (tileries and brickyards) until the early 20th Century in many locations of the departments Aube, Haute-Marne, Yonne and Meuse. Because of the end of their industrial exploitation, none of the historical outcrops of the Argiles à Plicatules is longer accessible.","environment":"marine indet.","primary_reference":"S. Bersac and D. Bert. 2015. Two ammonite species under the same name: Revision of Deshayesites deshayesi (d’Orbigny, 1841) based on topotype material (Lower Aptian, Lower Cretaceous, northeast of France). Annales de Paléontologie 101:265-294","phylum":"Mollusca","phylum_no":"7805","class":"Cephalopoda","class_no":"12315","order":"Ammonitida","order_no":"84931","family":"Deshayesitidae","family_no":"144188","genus":"Deshayesites","genus_no":"14761"},
