{"occurrence_no":"1444972","record_type":"occ","collection_no":"151252","identified_name":"Cartierodon cf. egerkingensis","identified_rank":"species","accepted_name":"Cartierodon egerkingensis","accepted_rank":"species","accepted_no":"387241","early_interval":"Lutetian","max_ma":48.07,"min_ma":41.03,"reference_no":"69037","lng":"4.750000","lat":"45.866669","cc":"FR","state":"Rhone","latlng_basis":"based on nearby landmark","latlng_precision":"minutes","geogcomments":"\"The locality no longer exists. It was located in a western extension of the Mont d’Or lyonnais, a small limestone mount located 10 km north-northwest of Lyon, central eastern France (‘‘département’’, or administrative region, of Rhône). The fossils were recovered from a fissure-fill situated close to the\r\nhamlet of La Clôtre, near the village of Lissieu. The enclosing rocks, and therefore the fissure disappeared (mined out) by the end of the nineteenth century.\" - Rage and Auge (2010)","environment":"fissure fill","primary_reference":"F. Solé and B. Mennecart. 2019. A large hyaenodont from the Lutetian of Switzerland expands the body mass range of the European mammalian predators during the Eocene. Acta Palaeontologica Polonica 64(2):275-290","phylum":"Chordata","phylum_no":"33815","class":"Mammalia","class_no":"36651","order":"Hyaenodonta","order_no":"253430","family":"Hyaenodontidae","family_no":"40903","genus":"Cartierodon","genus_no":"387240"},
