{"occurrence_no":"1484669","record_type":"occ","reid_no":"41989","collection_no":"203355","identified_name":"Apudites antiquus","identified_rank":"species","accepted_name":"Apudites antiquus","accepted_rank":"species","accepted_no":"179006","early_interval":"Anisian","max_ma":247,"min_ma":241.464,"reference_no":"89603","lng":"7.491667","lat":"48.577778","cc":"FR","state":"Grand Est","county":"Bas-Rhin","latlng_basis":"based on nearby landmark","latlng_precision":"seconds","geogscale":"outcrop","geogcomments":"\"‘Carriere royale’ quarry (‘Konigsgrube’) near Soultz-les-Bains (Sulzbad, west of Strasbourg; N 48°34'35'', E 7°29'30'').\" \"The quarry near Soultz-les Bains is the classical 19th century locality, from where Schimper’s material was collected, including several specimens described as Apudites antiquus (Schimper 1840, 1853, pl. 3), which were the earliest fossils subsequently attributed to the modern notostracan genus, Triops.\"","environment":"lacustrine - small","primary_reference":"G. Geyer, T. A. Hegna, and K. Kelber. 2024. The end of the ‘living fossil’ tale? A new look at Triassic specimens assigned to the tadpole shrimp Triops cancriformis (Notostraca) and associated phyllopods from the Vosges region (eastern France). Papers in Palaeontology 10(5):1-31","phylum":"Arthropoda","phylum_no":"18891","class":"Branchiopoda","class_no":"22113","order":"Notostraca","order_no":"133207","family":"NO_FAMILY_SPECIFIED","family_no":"NF","genus":"Apudites","genus_no":"179003"},
